<section class="evidence-band signal-chain-dossier" aria-labelledby="bench-order-heading">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label fi-caption-box"><span class="fi-prompt-marker" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>MINIMUM BENCH ORDER</p>
      <h2 id="bench-order-heading">INSPECT. IDENTIFY. ISOLATE. THEN APPLY POWER.</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="progression-list">
      <li class="active">
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Preserve</h3>
        <p>Photograph both sides, labels, sockets, and present configuration before cleaning or moving hardware.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Identify</h3>
        <p>Preserve the confirmed X99 CPU markings. Record exact graphics-card and water-block labels locally.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Inspect</h3>
        <p>Check sockets, power stages, connectors, residues, heat damage, missing components, and mounting hardware.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Bench</h3>
        <p>Use known-good power, one memory module, an air cooler, and only the display hardware required to reach firmware.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>05</span>
        <h3>Record</h3>
        <p>Capture diagnostic codes, CPU and memory detection, fan speed, temperatures, and every stop condition.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>06</span>
        <h3>Advance</h3>
        <p>Add storage, networking, firmware work, or liquid cooling only after the minimal configuration is stable.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

